<title>CANADA: Saskatchewan Agriculture details crop development.</title>
<headline>Saskatchewan Agriculture details crop development.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saskatchewan Agriculture on Tuesday detailed the level of crop development to Sunday.</p>
<p>CEREALS  TILLERED  JOINTED  SHOTBLADE HEADED SOFT DOUGH</p>
<p>July 13    1 pct     9 pct    42 pct   46 pct  2 pct</p>
<p>92/96 Avg  3 pct    19 pct    48 pct   29 pct  1 pct</p>
<p>CANOLA   EMERGED  SEEDLING  ROSETTE  FLOWERING PODDING</p>
<p>July 13    0 pct     1 pct    19 pct   73 pct  7 pct</p>
<p>92/96 Avg  0 pct     6 pct    34 pct   58 pct  2 pct</p>
<p>FLAX     EMERGED  SEEDLING  TILLERED FLOWERING BOLL</p>
<p>July 13    0 pct     5 pct    54 pct   40 pct  1 pct</p>
<p>92/96 Avg  0 pct    10 pct    71 pct   18 pct  0 pct</p>
<p>FALL CROP SHOTBLADE HEADED  DOUGH    RIPE</p>
<p>July 13    0 pct    20 pct    68 pct   12 pct</p>
<p>92/96 Avg  1 pct    27 pct    70 pct    2 pct</p>
<p>PULSE CRP VEGETATIVE   FLOWERING  PODDING</p>
<p>July 13    24 pct	  66 pct    10 pct</p>
<p>July 15/96 50 pct	  47 pct     3 pct</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
